# Agent memory: git push direction for this repository

Remote: git@github.com:kudumens/agentic-ai-practice.git (SSH, account kudumens)
Default branch: main. Branch protection on main is NOT enabled, so a pull
request is the only review gate. Never merge or push to main directly.

## Working method

Every phase is built in a dedicated git worktree, committed on its own
branch, pushed to origin, and raised as a pull request for human review.

    git worktree add .claude/worktrees/phase-{n}-{name}
    cd .claude/worktrees/phase-{n}-{name}
    git add . && git commit -m "..."
    git push origin phase-{n}-{name}
    gh pr create --base main --head phase-{n}-{name} --title "..." --body-file PR_BODY.md

## The gh CLI is the supported path, not manual browser steps

gh 2.102.0 is installed and authenticated as kudumens with the repo scope, so
pull requests are created from the terminal with `gh pr create`. Do not
leave the user to click through the GitHub UI.

    gh pr view <n> --json title,body,files
    gh pr list --state all
    gh pr diff <n>

Merging is left to the user: `gh pr merge <n> --squash` only after they
have reviewed it.

## Naming rules that prevent accidents

- The compose file is `compose.yaml` (PLAN.md section 9), not
  `docker-compose.yml`.
- Phase documents are named `PHASE{N}.md`. The root `README.md` is the
  project overview and hardware documentation; a phase branch must never
  overwrite it.
- Use Docker Compose v2 (`docker compose`). The `docker-compose` binary is
  the deprecated v1 form.
- Secrets live in `.env`, which is gitignored. `.env.example` is committed
  with empty values.
- The branch name is reused across phases only after its pull request is
  merged and the worktree removed.

